\tenuto is not a command that can be executed on its own.
It is highlighted in the editor, but running it gives an
"unknown command" error.

A tenuto is written after a note with two hyphens, like:

\bar ten-1 {
    \inst1 c'4-- d'-- e'2
}

A tenuto note sounds for a percentage of its duration,
90% by default. To change this percentage, use
\notedur.tenuto with an integer from 1 to 100:

\notedur.tenuto 95

This is applied to all instruments. See also \staccato
and \staccatissimo.
